,{"id":"note_hospitalist_history_and_physical_2026_10_20_07_15","type":"hp","title":"Hospitalist History and Physical","author":"S. Patel, MD","datetime":"2026-10-20 07:15","category":"H&P","summary":"Admission H&P for vitamin b12 deficiency anemia.","body":"**Chief complaint**\n- Fatigue and tingling in the hands and feet\n\n**History of present illness**\n66-year-old female with 3 months of worsening tiredness, a sore smooth tongue and tingling in the fingers and toes, now dizzy and unsteady when walking. Hemoglobin low with large red cells, vitamin B12 level 148 pg/mL (low). Admitted for intramuscular B12 replacement, folic acid and prevention of blood clots while less mobile.\n\n**Past medical history**\n- No significant past medical history.\n\n**Past surgical history**\n- No prior surgeries.\n\n**Home medications**\n- None\n\n**Allergies**\n- No known drug allergies.\n\n**Family history**\n- Mother with hypertension; father with coronary artery disease. No known family history of bowel disease or cancer.\n\n**Social history**\n- Lives with spouse/partner; independent with ADLs and ambulation at baseline; tobacco: never; alcohol: none; other substances: none.\n\n**Review of systems**\n- Positive for fatigue, tingling in the hands and feet, pale skin, unsteady walking and a sore tongue. Negative for chest pain, shortness of breath at rest, bleeding, black stools and weight loss.\n\n**Vitals**\n- T 98.2 F, HR 96, BP 125/77, RR 16, SpO2 99% on room air, pain 1/10 | Wt 62 kg, BMI 23.3\n\n**Physical exam**\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Pale, warm and dry; mildly jaundiced sclera.\n\n**Data**\n- Labs: Hemoglobin 9.4 (L)\n\n**Assessment and plan**\n66-year-old female with no significant history admitted with vitamin b12 deficiency anemia.\n\n**Vitamin B12 deficiency anemia**\n\n**Prophylaxis / code status**\n- DVT prophylaxis per orders; fall precautions.\n- Code status: Full Code."},{"id":"note_ed_provider_note_2026_10_20_06_03","type":"erVisitSummary","title":"ED Provider Note","author":"J. Whitaker, MD","datetime":"2026-10-20 06:03","category":"ED Note","summary":"66-year-old female presenting with fatigue and tingling in the hands and feet; admitted to Hospital Medicine.","body":"**Chief complaint**\n- Fatigue and tingling in the hands and feet\n\n**HPI**\n66-year-old female with 3 months of worsening tiredness, a sore smooth tongue and tingling in the fingers and toes, now dizzy and unsteady when walking. Hemoglobin low with large red cells, vitamin B12 level 148 pg/mL (low). Admitted for intramuscular B12 replacement, folic acid and prevention of blood clots while less mobile.\n\n**Past medical / surgical history**\n- Medical: No significant past medical history.\n- Surgical: No prior surgeries.\n\n**Allergies**\n- No known drug allergies.\n\n**Social history**\n- Lives with spouse/partner; independent with ADLs and ambulation at baseline; tobacco: never; alcohol: none; other substances: none.\n\n**Triage vitals**\n- T 98.4 F, HR 93, BP 123/77, RR 15, SpO2 97% on room air, pain 0/10\n\n**Exam**\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Pale, warm and dry; mildly jaundiced sclera.\n\n**ED results**\n- Labs: Hemoglobin 9.4 (L)\n\n**ED course**\n- 0445 folic acid 1 mg Oral\n- 0445 heparin 5,000 units Subcutaneous\n- 0445 cyanocobalamin (VITAMIN B12) 1,000 mcg Intramuscular\n\n**Assessment / disposition**\n- Vitamin B12 deficiency anemia. \n- Admit to Hospital Medicine (Dr. S. Patel); condition guarded but stable."}],"timeline":{"marDate":"Tuesday, October 20, 2026","marTimeSlots":["0800","0900","1000","1100","1200","1300","1400","1500"],"simulationStart":"2026-10-20 08:45","simulationEnd":"2026-10-20 16:45"},"simulationTasks":[],"triggers":[],"facultyBuilder":{"builderVersion":2,"inputs":{"name":"Linda Park","age":66,"sex":"Female","mrn":"SIM-30415","unit":"Medical-Surgical 2 East","room":"212-1","heightCm":163,"weightKg":62,"primary":"lpn_b12","hospitalDay":1,"simDate":"2026-10-20","startTime":"08:45","hx":[],"surg":[],"surgText":"","allergies":[],"codeStatus":"Full Code","social":{"tobacco":"Never","alcohol":"None","drugs":"None","living":"Lives with spouse/partner","function":"Independent","other":""},"studentLevel":"First-semester LPN","complexity":"simple","facultyNotes":"","id":"lpn_b12","desc":"PO folic acid, SubQ heparin, IM vitamin B12"}}}}